        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "A stack of pipes has 24 pipes in the bottom row, 22 in the next row, 20 in the next row and so on, with 6 pipes in the top row. How many pipes are in the stack altogether?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "150 pipes",
          "worked": "$a=24$, $d=-2$, $a_n=6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}a_n&=a+(n-1)d\\\\6&=24+(n-1)(-2)\\\\-18&=-2(n-1)\\\\n-1&=9\\\\n&=10\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}S_{10}&=\\frac{10}{2}[24+6]\\\\S_{10}&=5(30)\\\\S_{10}&=150\\end{align*}$$\nThere are 150 pipes.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-b4eae-p40-practice-slot-12-slot-12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Jai trains for a fun run. He runs 3 km in the first week, 4.5 km in the second week, 6 km in the third week and so on, up to 18 km in the final week. How far does he run altogether?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$115.5\\text{ km}$",
          "worked": "$a=3$, $d=1.5$, $a_n=18$.\n$$\\begin{align*}a_n&=a+(n-1)d\\\\18&=3+(n-1)(1.5)\\\\15&=1.5(n-1)\\\\n-1&=10\\\\n&=11\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}S_{11}&=\\frac{11}{2}[3+18]\\\\S_{11}&=\\frac{11}{2}(21)\\\\S_{11}&=115.5\\text{ km}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      }
    ]
